  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_019: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieves 0.639 acc / 0.620 F1. The evidence clearly establishes that multimodal + multiprofile + avgpool + weighted is the strongest design family, and that image encoder choice (resnet50 vs imagenet_vit_l) makes negligible difference (0.639 vs 0.635). The major untested design dimension is the RNA encoder: all multimodal experiments so far use pca_n2000 (a linear projection), while scvi_n200 and scgpt offer learned, nonlinear representations that may capture biological structure more effectively. Config_031 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) isolates the RNA encoder variable within the best-performing configuration, directly testing whether a learned single-cell representation can push performance beyond the PCA baseline. This is the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact remaining decision: if scvi improves on PCA, it opens a new optimization direction; if not, it confirms PCA sufficiency and redirects effort toward other levers. Under a limited budget, resolving this key architectural question is more informative than testing lower-impact variations (e.g., transformer+weighted, which is unlikely to beat avgpool given prior evidence)."
}

